    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM6-VUZr",
      "title": "fix: unset ETHERSCAN_API_KEY to avoid rate limiting during simulations",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 1351,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Fixes slow simulation times (30+ minutes → ~35 seconds) for users with `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` set\r\n- Adds `unset ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` to all 7 recipes that run `forge script` with fork mode\r\n\r\n## Root Cause\r\n\r\nWhen `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` is set, Foundry fetches contract ABIs from Etherscan for every contract it interacts with during fork simulation. With a free-tier API key (5 calls/sec rate limit), this causes severe slowdowns.\r\n\r\nBy unsetting the key, Foundry skips Etherscan fetching and works directly with on-chain bytecode, which is all that's needed for simulations.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- [ ] Run `export ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=your_key && just simulate-stack eth` and verify it completes in a few minutes instead of 30+ minutes\r\n- [ ] Verify the user's shell environment still has `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` set after the command completes (since each recipe runs in a subshell)\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-21T00:01:07Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-01-21T00:20:50Z",
      "additions": 7,
      "deletions": 0
    },
